Add wolfSSL crypto backend (OpenSSL compat layer)

Adds `wolfssl` as a selectable crypto_backend (-Dcrypto_backend=wolfssl).
It reuses crypto_openssl.c built against wolfSSL's OpenSSL compatibility
layer (libwolfssl needs --enable-opensslall); crypto_wolfssl.c is a thin
shim that includes it.

wolfSSL does not report a usable OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER, so pretend to be
OpenSSL 1.1.1: no legacy shims, no EVP_MD_fetch(), no ENGINE.

Recent wolfSSL (5.9.x) returns a SubjectPublicKeyInfo from i2d_PublicKey()
where OpenSSL returns the bare key material, which changes the key id and
makes every signature UNTRUSTED. Compute the id from the unwrapped
subjectPublicKey instead.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -28,6 +28,9 @@ if get_option('crypto_backend') == 'openssl'
 	crypto_dep = dependency('openssl')
 elif get_option('crypto_backend') == 'mbedtls'
 	crypto_dep = [ dependency('mbedtls'), dependency('mbedcrypto') ]
+elif get_option('crypto_backend') == 'wolfssl'
+	crypto_dep = dependency('wolfssl')
+	add_project_arguments('-DAPK_CRYPTO_WOLFSSL', language: 'c')
 endif
 
 apk_deps = [ crypto_dep, zlib_dep, libzstd_dep ]
